{"gene":"NOTCH2","uniprot":"Q04721","proteinName":"neurogenic locus notch homolog protein 2 isoform 1 preproprotein","function":"Functions as a receptor for membrane-bound ligands Jagged-1 (JAG1), Jagged-2 (JAG2) and Delta-1 (DLL1) to regulate cell-fate determination. Upon ligand activation through the released notch intracellular domain (NICD) it forms a transcriptional activator complex with RBPJ/RBPSUH and activates genes of the enhancer of split locus. Affects the implementation of differentiation, proliferation and apoptotic programs. Involved in bone remodeling and homeostasis. In collaboration with RELA/p65 enhances NFATc1 promoter activity and positively regulates RANKL-induced osteoclast differentiation. Positively regulates self-renewal of liver cancer cells","pathwayComment":null,"pathways":[{"id":"R-HSA-9976102","name":"Differentiation of naive CD4+ T cells to T helper 2 cells (Th2 cells)","evidence":"IEA","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9945266","name":"Differentiation of T cells","evidence":"IEA","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-3906995","name":"Diseases associated with O-glycosylation of proteins","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-3781865","name":"Diseases of glycosylation","evidence":"TAS","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-5668914","name":"Diseases of metabolism","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-212436","name":"Generic Transcription Pathway","evidence":"TAS","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-350054","name":"Notch-HLH transcription pathway","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-2979096","name":"NOTCH2 Activation and Transmission of Signal to the Nucleus","evidence":"IEA","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-2197563","name":"NOTCH2 intracellular domain regulates transcription","evidence":"IEA","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9013695","name":"NOTCH4 Intracellular Domain Regulates Transcription","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-1912422","name":"Pre-NOTCH Expression an